{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777710-changeling-real-world-problems","id":777710,"title":"Changeling: Real world problems","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-01T06:17:40-08:00","id":777710,"title":"Changeling: Real world problems","content":"Hi. I used to play Changeling back in the day and often in mixed campaigns. My frustration with them is how useless they are in the real world. Yes, like anyone else they have attributes and skills, but the powers themselves were always such a hassle to get to work outside the dreaming. Do we have any reason to believe this has improved with C20 on the way? Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8508-phaide","name":"Phaide","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T07:07:32-08:00","id":777739,"title":"","content":"Yep. From a <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/shattered-smothered-covered-chunked-diced-peppered-capped-and-topped-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">Monday Meeting blog post</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matthew McFarland</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making changelings a bit more magically impressive is a priority, yes..</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T23:50:05-08:00","id":778143,"title":"","content":"My quick fix for this was to drop the difficulty from Banality + 4 to just Banality on its own. The average human is Banality 7, and a level one Bunk reduces the difficulty by one, so it'd make the average cantrip difficulty 6 to use on/around humans, which seems pretty acceptable. <br /> <br /> Glamour is also the other issue. It's scarce by its very nature. Most games I've seen have houseruled it by making dross more readily available, or players have just been more creative (that chimera we just killed? I'm gonna eat it's flesh for extra Glamour). I'm looking forward to seeing how C20 handles this, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T09:50:07-08:00","id":778404,"title":"","content":"Yeah, hopefully either they can store more Glamour or they can harvest it more easily, so that they can actually use their powers more than once a month or so in game-time. Heck, increasing both would be nice. Alternatively, decreasing their need for it to effect their cantrips in the real world would work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T18:14:16-08:00","id":778727,"title":"","content":"Yes, this has always been something endemic in both changeling games. I won't go as far as calling them useless, but I will say that compared with the other supernaturals they are fairly limited. I'm really happy that they are going to give them more juice in both lines. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T01:54:51-08:00","id":778863,"title":"","content":"Most other splats get a kind of 'meditation' roll to regain power, too (and vamps get 'hunting' as an abstract roll). Changelings can draw Glamour from a Balefire, but the amounts are so tiny it's not quite the same thing.<br /> <br /> To emulate this, in some games I've just allowed changelings to roll an appropriate Attribute + Ability to regain Glamour in the pursuit of creativity. But, like any other kind of meditation, the changeling has to spend time at it (points regained were capped by hours spent being creative). This does make Reverie mostly redundant so it will change the flavour of the game. <br /> <br /> However, Reverie could still be used to create dross or, more appropriately, sources of regular Glamour (artworks that, when they are witnessed by a new person, inspire a little more Glamour every time, and thus become a sort of Glamour battery the changeling can draw from over a longer term).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 12-03-2015, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T03:59:20-08:00","id":779677,"title":"","content":"i've thought of doing a rules hack similar to exalted's stunt rules, basically if the changeling can pull of something that fits with the 'rule of cool' in front of mortals with out using magic they can regain small amount of glamour by being creatures of wonder and adventure. obviously the specifics would vary from changeling to changeling, but its kind of something to help the players stay invested narratively and reward them for doing what changelings are supposed to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}